      "summaries": {
        "en": "FreeMoCap is an open-source motion capture system that democratizes 3D body tracking by using multiple standard webcams instead of expensive specialized hardware. Its core innovation lies in computer vision algorithms that triangulate 2D pose estimates from different camera angles into accurate 3D skeletal models in real time. Researchers and developers can use it for animation, biomechanics analysis, or human-computer interaction projects by setting up a multi-camera rig and processing the captured movement data through its Python pipeline.",
        "zh": "FreeMoCap 是一个开源运动捕捉系统，它通过多台普通网络摄像头实现三维人体动作追踪，让这项技术不再依赖昂贵专业设备。其核心技术在于计算机视觉算法：从不同视角的二维姿态估计中三角测量出精确的三维骨骼模型，并实时处理。用户只需搭建多摄像头阵列，就能通过 Python 流程捕获运动数据，适用于动画制作、生物力学分析或人机交互研究，为创意和技术实验提供了易用的工具。",
        "es": "FreeMoCap is an open-source motion capture system that democratizes 3D body tracking by using multiple standard webcams instead of expensive specialized hardware. Its core innovation lies in computer vision algorithms that triangulate 2D pose estimates from different camera angles into accurate 3D skeletal models in real time. Researchers and developers can use it for animation, biomechanics analysis, or human-computer interaction projects by setting up a multi-camera rig and processing the captured movement data through its Python pipeline.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "freemocap gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "FreeMoCap is an open-source motion capture system that democratizes 3D body tracking by using multiple standard webcams instead of expensive specialized hardware. Its core innovation lies in computer vision algorithms that triangulate 2D pose estimates from different camera angles into accurate 3D skeletal models in real time. Researchers and developers can use it for animation, biomechanics analysis, or human-computer interaction projects by setting up a multi-camera rig and processing the captured movement data through its Python pipeline.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/freemocap/freemocap for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
